  "description": "Cross-platform, self-contained HLSL Effect compiler for MonoGame, KNI, and FNA. Compiles .fx (or .slang, the HLSL-compatible subset of Slang) shaders to .mgfx binaries (MonoGame/KNI) or D3D9 fx_2_0 .fxb binaries (FNA) in memory at runtime — on Linux, macOS, or Windows — with no Wine, Windows SDK, fxc.exe, or mgfxc required. Also converts .fx pixel shaders to SkSL for SkiaSharp's SKRuntimeEffect and to raylib glsl330 fragment shaders for Raylib-cs (RaylibConverter). Add the package and call EffectCompiler.CompileAsync; feed the bytes to new Effect(gd, bytes). Pulls the ShadowDusk.* set and the native DXC + SPIRV-Cross + vkd3d-shader binaries transitively.",
  "id": "ShadowDusk.Compiler",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-05T07:23:27.043Z",
